WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.165
Week 5: Location, Condition, and Existence. locate a place describe a temporary condition say what is available

2
00:00:08.165 --> 00:00:18.337
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Use estar for location and temporary condition, and hay (from haber) for existence — they are not interchangeable.

3
00:00:18.337 --> 00:00:44.425
Model set. El banco está entre la farmacia y la tienda. Hay una silla al lado de la mesa. Los libros están encima del escritorio. No hay nadie dentro de la oficina. Estamos fuera del edificio. The bank is between the pharmacy and the store. There is a chair next to the table. The books are on top of the desk. There is no one inside the office. We are outside the building.

4
00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:54.576
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:54.576 --> 00:01:06.946
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: locate a place; describe a temporary condition; say what is available. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:06.946 --> 00:01:33.865
Model language. El banco está entre la farmacia y la tienda. — The bank is between the pharmacy and the store. Hay una silla al lado de la mesa. — There is a chair next to the table. Los libros están encima del escritorio. — The books are on top of the desk. No hay nadie dentro de la oficina. — There is no one inside the office. Estamos fuera del edificio. — We are outside the building.

7
00:01:33.865 --> 00:01:43.763
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
